{
  "$comment": "GENERATED. The runtime reads this to build the layer/view UI and apply themes.",
  "groups": [
    {
      "id": "water",
      "label": "Water",
      "toggleable": false,
      "defaultVisible": true
    },
    {
      "id": "depth",
      "label": "Lake depth",
      "toggleable": true,
      "defaultVisible": false
    },
    {
      "id": "protected",
      "label": "Parks and reserves",
      "toggleable": true,
      "defaultVisible": false,
      "$comment": "Off by default. Parks and ecological reserves are large opaque areas and they buried the water they sit around — the map's job is to say which water is open, and an overlay that hides the water fails at it. Behind Layers."
    },
    {
      "id": "access",
      "label": "Land access",
      "toggleable": true,
      "defaultVisible": false,
      "$comment": "Off by default, for the same reason as `protected`: these are big fills, and the answer is the water. A user who needs to know where they may not go turns it on, and then it is the point of the screen rather than noise on it."
    },
    {
      "id": "admin",
      "label": "Management units",
      "toggleable": true,
      "defaultVisible": false
    }
  ],
  "views": [
    {
      "id": "regulations",
      "label": "Regulations",
      "default": true,
      "modes": {
        "stream": "closure",
        "under_lake": "plain",
        "lake": "closure",
        "wetland": "plain",
        "contour": "plain",
        "park": "plain",
        "eco_reserve": "plain",
