        "data": {
          "provider": "regs",
          "field": "status",
          "params": [
            "date",
            "species"
          ]
        },
        "$comment": "`missing` is the colour of water the app has said NOTHING about — no feature-state has been pushed for it. It was color.status.open, so every unevaluated feature in the province rendered as open: the single most dangerous wrong answer this app can give, and the failure rule 29 exists to prevent. It is now the neutral no-data colour. 'Open under the general rules' is a real answer the app computes and pushes; it is not the same thing as not having looked."
      },
      "standing": {
        "label": "Flow for the date",
        "scale": "continuous",
        "property": "standing",
        "stops": [
          [
            -1,
            {
              "token": "color.flow.nobaseline"
            }
          ],
          [
            0,
            {
              "token": "color.flow.f1"
            }
          ],
          [
            16.7,
            {
              "token": "color.flow.f2"
            }
          ],
          [
            33.3,
            {
              "token": "color.flow.f3"
            }
          ],
          [
            50,
            {
              "token": "color.flow.f4"
            }
          ],
          [
            66.7,
            {
              "token": "color.flow.f5"
            }
          ],
          [
            83.3,
            {
              "token": "color.flow.f6"
            }
          ],
          [
            100,
            {
              "token": "color.flow.f7"
            }
          ]
        ],
        "missing": {
          "token": "color.water.unmapped"
        },
        "data": {
          "provider": "gauges",
          "field": "standing"
        },
        "$comment": "The PERCENTILE for this day of year, not the discharge: 15.7 m3/s is a flood on one creek and a drought on another. `missing` is neutral water, never status.unknown — most reaches have no gauge entitled to speak for them, and that is not the same as a rule we could not parse.  SEVEN STOPS, and they ARE the legend's: the ramp was three tokens that all resolved to shades of one blue while the legend beside it drew red through cyan — two definitions of one scale (AGENTS rule 23). The legend now reads these tokens.  MISSING is `water.unmapped`, the pale grey, NOT `water.mapped`, which is a saturated teal darker than the low-flow end and made ungauged water read as more prominent than measured water. 97.6% of BC has no gauge: it must stay visible and stay quiet.  A STOP AT -1 IS A SENTINEL. It means the reach HAS a working gauge but no historical record to compare today against — 8 of BC's reporting stations, and before it existed they painted identically to water nobody measures, which is the wrong claim in the other direction. Real percentiles are 0..100, so nothing ever interpolates across the gap between -1 and 0."
      }
    },
